<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="5f8b2097">&lt;p&gt;
    Development and execution of an appropriate cutover and deployment plan is an important activity undertaken to
    facilitate a successful transition.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The plan is used to guide transition activities, drive realization of benefits, provide the project maintains an
    appropriate level of visibility and momentum and help the cutover and deployment team determine the level of risk
    inherent in the proposed approach.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    A comprehensive plan helps determine transition leadership, assign a project team and document roles and
    responsibilities. It helps define organization structure, reporting relationships, escalation paths and decision-making
    processes. It defines the transition command structure, tools and repositories. The plan defines metrics that
    demonstrate success of cutover and deployment activities.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="6fbdd1cc"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="27e95804">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Plan the program as an integrated set of projects; map and manage dependencies among the projects
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Include all stakeholders and consider the activities for which they will be responsible
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Provide appropriate training for stakeholders so they will be able to successfully complete their responsibilities
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Fully engage business and IT managers with stakeholders throughout the transition period
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Consider appropriate communication mechanisms and messaging levels for different stakeholder audiences
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Focus on areas such as systems and interface development, scope change, recruitment, site setup, level of clean-up
        needed and knowledge transfer
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="73ab4b84"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="c862c65c">To define the activities, milestones and sequence necessary to cut over and deploy the solution into a production
environment.</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="c1d5724f"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="524aced9"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="9920b5a3">&lt;p&gt;
    A typical cutover and deployment plan includes:  
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Roles and responsibilities of transition leadership 
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Roles and responsibilities of the transition team
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Definition of business and technology transition activities
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Definition of tools and repositories to support the transition
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Steps to set up a centralized command structure
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        An organization structure with reporting lines
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        A governance structure with escalation and decision-making processes
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Definition of success measures
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Schedule of when the transition activities are to be performed
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Individual project or workstream team role assignments, responsibilities and schedules&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="representationOptions" nodeId="8a95ed36"></attribute>
